   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The interval \\( 2 \\le t \\le 10 \\) uses the rows at t = 2 and t = 10, so the change in D is \\( 60 - 29 = 31 \\).",
         "mathjson": 31,
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99005",
         "rule_named": "difference of tabulated values"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Dividing by the change in time, \\( D'(4) \\approx \\frac{D(10) - D(2)}{10 - 2} = \\frac{60 - 29}{10 - 2} = \\frac{31}{8} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            31,
